Z||000000||JetroGT||10-25-2001||11:30 PM||||The last time I painted the valve covers on a fiero the metal didn't stay shiney, so this time I painted everything.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1and2.jpg">  <P>This time around I'm going for a two tone paint job. Something that covers all the metal but still brings out the lines.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3and4_1.jpg"> <P>So what do you think? Is it too ricey?<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cover5.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||AutoXdbdragSE||10-26-2001||12:19 AM||||Do the valve covers paint ad horse power?<BR>If yes, Yeah that's rice.<BR>If no.. those are hella sweet.. i like how they look, it's not paint brushed aluminum, but paint with a patter.. hella hella cool.. i wanna see the whole thing when you are done.. good luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||10-26-2001||12:43 AM||||I'm masking the front cover now. I think it will look good. The car that this stuff is going into needs a paint job. 87 GT with a blown motor. It's an arazona car. I checked the trunk. No rust, never wrecked. After this I'll have to save up again untill spring to get the thing painted. Untill then it will be fast and ugly. ||||reg||1
